# Roots to add to Mozilla's list (tools/make_ca_bundle.py), as PEM certificates below this comment.
#
# The frame only looks up the issuer of the LAST certificate the server sends. If a server's chain
# ends in a cross-signed root whose issuer Mozilla no longer lists, browsers still trust it but the
# frame won't: `make_ca_bundle.py --check <host>` then names the missing root to paste in here.
# Netlify's Let's Encrypt chains need nothing extra.
